This lists known issue with dependencies and such.

Libfaketime 0.99.7 has a bug that can cause segfaults during testbench
runs. If you experience them, either use --disable-libfaketime configure
switch or go back to an older version.
see also: https://github.com/rsyslog/rsyslog/issues/2099

On Solaris 11 x64 (SunStudio build), several disk-assisted (DA) queue tests
hang at shutdown until the 580 s abort timeout: segmented-da-tcp-spill-exact,
segmented-da-idle-timeout-values, and the ruleset/action scenarios of
classic-da-behavior and segmented-da-behavior. They are skipped on SunOS.
The root cause is not yet known; remove the skips once it is fixed.
see also: https://github.com/rsyslog/rsyslog/issues/7917
